ogles2: v3d's interpolateAtOffset honours the offset without MSAA too.
load_interpolated_input returned the pre-computed (pixel centre) value when
the fragment key has no msaa, so interpolateAtOffset into a single-sample
target ignored its offset (dEQP-GLES31 multisample_interpolation's
interpolate_at_offset on the default framebuffer and single-sample
textures and renderbuffers; Mesa's v3d does not offer
OES_shader_multisample_interpolation, so its CI does not run them). The
input's raw varying is kept either way (emit_fragment_varying), and in a
single-sample job the sample is the pixel centre: the result is centre +
offset. Only interpolateAt* produce load_interpolated_input (v3d lowers
them, lower_interpolate_at; other inputs are load_input).

--- a/src/broadcom/compiler/nir_to_vir.c
+++ b/src/broadcom/compiler/nir_to_vir.c
@@ -4019,12 +4019,15 @@
                                 (nir_intrinsic_base(instr) + offset) * 4 +
                                 nir_intrinsic_component(instr) + i;
 
-                        /* If we are not in MSAA or if we are not interpolating
-                         * a user varying, just return the pre-computed
-                         * interpolated input.
+                        /* If we are not interpolating a user varying, just
+                         * return the pre-computed interpolated input.
+                         * ogles2: without MSAA too, interpolateAtOffset's
+                         * offset applies (the sample is the pixel centre,
+                         * so this is centre + offset; dEQP-GLES31
+                         * multisample_interpolation on single-sample
+                         * targets).
                          */
-                        if (!c->fs_key->msaa ||
-                            c->interp[input_idx].vp.file == QFILE_NULL) {
+                        if (c->interp[input_idx].vp.file == QFILE_NULL) {
                                 ntq_store_def(c, &instr->def, i,
                                               vir_MOV(c, c->inputs[input_idx]));
                                 continue;
